{"code": "const msg = `Interim status (full report follows; bot restart + round trip is the last step, tests green 1067 passed).

(1) Bot: NOT yet proven end to end after my fix. Evidence of the break: infra-daemons log D:\\Projects\\AHome\\local-vault\\logs\\telegram-gateway.stderr.log shows Ahmed's real message at 16:07:59 handled (intent=chat effort=fast) but the local core asked Ollama for "qwen3:8b", which is NOT installed (HTTP 404 "model 'qwen3:8b' not found" - I reproduced it directly), so every reply was the canned UNAVAILABLE text. That is the owner's "canned replies" complaint. Fixed in domain/ai_profiles.py (all four efforts now qwen3.5:9b); restart + real send in progress.

(2) Numbers now: RAM total 23.78 GB. Before/after load measured today: free 7.41 GB -> 4.22 GB with qwen3.5:9b resident (6.65 GB model, 3.31 GB of it in VRAM, rest CPU/mmap). Generation 11.3 tok/s at 16384 ctx, 13.3 tok/s at small ctx. Settings settled: OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=2, OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=1, OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=16384, FLASH_ATTENTION=1, KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0 (user env vars, verified). Also found and killed a SECOND Ollama server on 11434 (started by SIR Laptop Manager ops_ui, pid 7548) that was the actual 127.0.0.1 listener with a copy of the model in RAM; that alone gave ~3 GB back. Worth telling the Laptop Manager owner to stop spawning it.

(3) Thinking level: site setting is the effort menu Auto/Fast/Balanced/Think deeper (apps/web/src/components/studio/AiEffortMenu.tsx -> mode on the job). Key mapping: AHome/apps/local-core/domain/ai_profiles.py THINK_BY_EFFORT = fast "low", balanced "medium", deeper "high", code "high", sent as the "think" field of /api/chat by data/smart_ai_router.py (verified Ollama 0.40.16 accepts string levels; thinking arrives in message.thinking so answers stay clean).

(4) Light models, background only, CPU (num_gpu 0), 30s keep_alive, RAM-gated: qwen3:4b for classify/tag/summarize, nemotron-3-nano:4b for automations. New file data/background_models.py refuses roles chat/code/coding/reply. gemma4:e4b deliberately unused (as big as the chat model). Docs: D:\\Projects\\AHome\\docs\\LOCAL_MODELS.md.`;
console.log(JSON.stringify(await tools.send_message({target:"lead", message: msg})));
", "description": "Send interim status to lead"}

